Experiment No.: 8

Title

Demonstration of Interrupts in Arduino

Aim

To demonstrate hardware interrupts using Arduino.

Theory

Interrupts allow Arduino to respond immediately to external events without continuously checking the input condition.

Components Required
Arduino Uno
Push Button
Jumper Wires
Procedure
Connect push button to interrupt pin 2.
Write interrupt service routine.
Upload the program.
Press the button.
Observe interrupt count.
Code
volatile int count=0;

void interruptFunction()
{
  count++;
}

void setup()
{
  Serial.begin(9600);
  pinMode(2,INPUT_PULLUP);

  attachInterrupt(
  digitalPinToInterrupt(2),
  interruptFunction,
  FALLING);
}

void loop()
{
  Serial.println(count);
  delay(1000);
}
Output

Interrupt count increases when the button is pressed.

Result

Interrupt functionality was successfully demonstrated.

Conclusion

Arduino interrupt operation was studied successfully.
